axis: absence-representation
axis_gloss: "how a missing value is shown: a named marker saying what is absent and why, or an empty string, null or omitted key"
poles:
  a: explicit-typed-absence
  b: silent-blank
split: lone-exception
draft_status: axis-only
leverage: 6.7
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(14) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  On absence representation — how a missing value is shown: a named marker
  saying what is absent and why, or an empty string, null or omitted key — the
  records assert both explicit typed absence (13 judgments, 4 authored) and
  silent blank (1 judgments, 0 authored). Which should be the stated rule, and
  where is the exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

